{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>And I will walk, etc., in keri.</b> That is, He will not bring upon them directed sufferings corresponding to their sin as He did beforehand — for previously He would bring [suffering] commensurate with their sin, on the principle of (Psalms 62:12) ״תְּשַׁלֵּם לְאִישׁ כְּמַעֲשֵׂהוּ״ — since this would awaken a slumbering heart, and they would understand to improve the deeds against which the evil had come upon them. But HaShem said: if they walk with Him in keri and fail to discern the deed of HaShem — that He is awakening their heart through directed suffering corresponding to their sins — then He too will walk with them in keri and bring upon them sufferings that bear no resemblance to their evil deeds. And these are: sword, siege, pestilence, deliverance into the hand of an enemy, and famine — which comprises three troubles — altogether seven."], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:02:20.384367552Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}